One of the cool things about Nethack is that even if you've read the
source and understand it, the game can still be challenging.  A
perfectly spoiled player will still not win 100% of the time, though he
might win 99% of it.

And while it's possible to win without encountering (out-of-game)
spoilers, it will probably take you at least years to do it.  Also
consider: it took me years to win my first time and I was a voracious
reader of spoilers.  And a lot of Nethack's cooler things will probably
never unveil themselves before a non-spoiled player.

Even so, unless it's a thread that's obviously spoily (YAAPs, YANIs,
patch stuff, source divings, design discussions) it's probably a good
idea to try to mark spoiler stuff in your posts, if you can bother
yourself with it.  So much that goes on here falls under one of those
categories, however, that players who want to maintain perfect
ignorance (is that even possible with Nethack?) are probably better off
not reading the group, just in case.

